From 324934909836d1ea0d8e7949268cf62a115ce278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@local>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:05:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] V100/CUDA 11.8 port: sm_70 floor, IQ4_XS selftest,
 Volta setup path, Windows compile fixes

- CMake: allow sm_70+ (was sm_80+), CUDA C++17 for nvcc 11.8, shared
  cudart (fixes LNK2005), enable_testing so ctest parity works,
  native_expert_parity --selftest registered.
- Kernels: IQ4_XS (type 23) synthetic --selftest in
  native_expert_parity (no GGUF needed); sm_70 QSA fallback path.
- setup.py: per-GPU CUDA selection (cu11 wheels / driver 452+ /
  toolkit 11.8 on Volta, upstream cu13 otherwise), nvidia-smi
  fallback for old drivers without compute_cap query.
- Windows/CUDA 11.8 compile fixes: 5-arg cudaGraphInstantiate,
  cudaSetDeviceFlags instead of cudaInitDevice (remote_experts),
  device arch floor message.
